:db/id "q-66279" :question/id #uuid "73389b95-3445-5532-a631-3954ade47917" :question/math-academy-id "q-66279" :question/problem "Solve the equation $\\,{x}^{2}+5=-2x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write the equation in standard form by bringing all of the terms to the left-hand side. This gives the equation\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+2x+5=0.\n$$\n\nWe can find the roots of a quadratic equation using the quadratic formula:\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{-b\\pm \\sqrt{{b}^{2}-4ac}}{2a}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the coefficients are $a=1,\\,b=2,$ and $c=5.$ Substituting these values into the quadratic formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{-2\\pm \\sqrt{{2}^{2}-4(1)(5)}}{2(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2\\pm \\sqrt{4-20}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2\\pm \\sqrt{-16}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2\\pm 4\\,\\text{i}}{2} \\\\  & =-1\\pm 2\\,\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has two solutions, $x=-1+2\\,\\text{i}$ and $x=-1-2\\,\\text{i}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-66279/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef8dec7d-5154-59ee-aee8-9f068eb6b8f4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-66279"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-66435/selection/d5c1bee19489cd750285a5cad9846824691266fb793ae56261a26f694263dadc" :answer/id #uuid "ef877427-20e1-5da3-8f68-7602e66b9e88" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p+q=-92,\\,x=-8\\pm 10\\,\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-66435/selection/db7849f7f83d8a4621b457232cc6052b189e6deb40224d7e5b213fe956140953" :answer/id #uuid "d04c5f56-6884-54db-b2d5-48253abb7029" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p+q=-92,\\,x=10\\pm 8\\,\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-66435/selection/4919af76dccaab8c215418530f7dd6af548294f75ab4590476b745ad99f585ba" :answer/id #uuid "abcca7a5-ad85-5c0a-a260-ff19bd9ad4e4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p+q=-108,\\,x=10\\pm 8\\,\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-66435/selection/539a373890941c676619697ee6526acbe9741fcc6d7f9d29fe0b2fade473c5fd" :answer/id #uuid "7ea322bd-0b73-5606-8256-43216ddc26d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p+q=-108,\\,x=-8\\pm 10\\,\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-66435/selection/f84537ef14ab729ad0370904b6539e1f9f0bc510717967a4f2635bd77f781aa5" :answer/id #uuid "c82e3d79-83fb-5dc0-a4d6-69fe641c382a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p+q=-92,\\,x=-8\\pm 8\\,\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-66435/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "107fc32d-7a9a-5596-b677-da1106e9c1fc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-66435/selection/d5c1bee19489cd750285a5cad9846824691266fb793ae56261a26f694263dadc" :answer-field/choices ["q-66435/selection/d5c1bee19489cd750285a5cad9846824691266fb793ae56261a26f694263dadc" "q-66435/selection/db7849f7f83d8a4621b457232cc6052b189e6deb40224d7e5b213fe956140953" "q-66435/selection/4919af76dccaab8c215418530f7dd6af548294f75ab4590476b745ad99f585ba" "q-66435/selection/539a373890941c676619697ee6526acbe9741fcc6d7f9d29fe0b2fade473c5fd" "q-66435/selection/f84537ef14ab729ad0370904b6539e1f9f0bc510717967a4f2635bd77f781aa5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-66435" :question/id #uuid "f70143e0-3f9c-51d2-946d-0c2579968816" :question/math-academy-id "q-66435" :question/problem "The equation ${x}^{2}+16x+164=0$ can be written in the form $(x+p)^{2}=q.$ Find $p+q,$ and solve the equation." :question/worked-solution "We first move the constant to the right-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+16x+164 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+16x & =-164\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we complete the square on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+16x & =-164 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2\\cdot 8x+{8}^{2}-{8}^{2} & =-164 \\\\ (x+8)^{2}-64 & =-164 \\\\ (x+8)^{2} & =-100\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=8,\\,q=-100,$ and $p+q=-92.$\n\nWe now solve the equation using the square root method.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+8)^{2} & =-100 \\\\ x+8 & =\\pm \\sqrt{-100} \\\\ x+8 & =\\pm 10\\,\\text{i} \\\\ x & =-8\\pm 10\\,\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has two solutions, $x=-8+10\\,\\text{i}$ and $x=-8-10\\,\\text{i}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-66435/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a9c8c1d8-2662-5c15-b084-084f9e930141"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-66435"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-66791/selection/2103d3f5714f4f3b29abe786040d09abfe3e31df6a3691dcf08e740bedf03097" :answer/id #uuid "a8d6de65-4859-5f83-89f1-dba6646abbd6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=2\\pm 2\\,\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-66791/selection/85254645fe0426771b22622a5c96ff8416444b7c27a1481a71db30318a18f5a4" :answer/id #uuid "44778d4c-5910-5968-a817-c753aee3d315" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=2\\pm 7\\,\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-66791/selection/636fc91a59fb1aa0b599e5816cedc5a64f7225ea3b34c66e70674d0c8b76f82e" :answer/id #uuid "4e329fcf-7d2c-5c43-83e2-757be955a47d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-2\\pm 7\\,\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-66791/selection/8fc73997e2e0f931eb38f18e5ebf2559225b767a25ba5d3598f8075e249fd60d" :answer/id #uuid "f42a2d13-7b45-5781-9afb-e2e8ebdb884a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=4\\pm 7\\,\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-66791/selection/cf5e5a66074e0434f8235feda29cb182ac4b60bab2dff0677f7b365ca9732d21" :answer/id #uuid "d79c00dd-0063-5d69-b2c8-c0198ba16625" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-2\\pm 2\\,\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-66791/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d5c4c9e3-6cca-59a0-a8c9-93fef2194a06" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-66791/selection/85254645fe0426771b22622a5c96ff8416444b7c27a1481a71db30318a18f5a4" :answer-field/choices ["q-66791/selection/2103d3f5714f4f3b29abe786040d09abfe3e31df6a3691dcf08e740bedf03097" "q-66791/selection/85254645fe0426771b22622a5c96ff8416444b7c27a1481a71db30318a18f5a4" "q-66791/selection/636fc91a59fb1aa0b599e5816cedc5a64f7225ea3b34c66e70674d0c8b76f82e" "q-66791/selection/8fc73997e2e0f931eb38f18e5ebf2559225b767a25ba5d3598f8075e249fd60d" "q-66791/selection/cf5e5a66074e0434f8235feda29cb182ac4b60bab2dff0677f7b365ca9732d21"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-66791" :question/id #uuid "fdebaefd-71be-50d5-afa2-969c275d27ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-66791" :question/problem "What are the solutions of the equation $(x-2)^{2}=-49?$" :question/worked-solution "The left-hand side is a perfect square. Therefore, we can solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)^{2} & =-49 \\\\ x-2 & =\\pm \\sqrt{-49} \\\\ x-2 & =\\pm 7\\,\\text{i} \\\\ x & =2\\pm 7\\,\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has two solutions, $x=2+7\\,\\text{i}$ and $x=2-7\\,\\text{i}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-66791/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a9c8c1d8-2662-5c15-b084-084f9e930141"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-66791"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-113245/selection/49053fd8b49cd1fcd9bb38fc30b5c5de3038bc0273d3aba53c51d3e8a5f8dfa3" :answer/id #uuid "5ab819f1-b137-5387-ba0e-b180c9c1d7ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p+q=22,\\,x=3\\pm 5\\,\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113245/selection/7c5b20195a3ec7b074300fa420393ddee4734e7e1fa089e2352f78a7188b789e" :answer/id #uuid "793b92be-55a7-56d9-b512-1e28798469d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p+q=22,\\,x=5\\pm 3\\,\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113245/selection/5e9b625d4cdfd50931e6256d13df63e909e67d24a16ceb2dd816381e072bf2c8" :answer/id #uuid "a5d13c9a-48d1-53f6-9cae-598b61d7a27a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p+q=-28,\\,x=5\\pm 3\\,\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113245/selection/e07c611192af075822ecf1844fc9b9bd50dbccd83259e0c40b56147e9677b780" :answer/id #uuid "6f1c338d-65fc-5d38-a8df-44f75f4fd14b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p+q=-28,\\,x=3\\pm 3\\,\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113245/selection/2b6b5b63fb8ecaea967cd7ac2863ce8bd58656d3ccc4ec1b14aec4077dcfb3c4" :answer/id #uuid "ec31137e-54bd-5fae-a80a-ec5cc7564743" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p+q=-28,\\,x=3\\pm 5\\,\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113245/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "835d29e0-8e70-5cbf-a186-51ba6e696c1e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-113245/selection/2b6b5b63fb8ecaea967cd7ac2863ce8bd58656d3ccc4ec1b14aec4077dcfb3c4" :answer-field/choices ["q-113245/selection/49053fd8b49cd1fcd9bb38fc30b5c5de3038bc0273d3aba53c51d3e8a5f8dfa3" "q-113245/selection/7c5b20195a3ec7b074300fa420393ddee4734e7e1fa089e2352f78a7188b789e" "q-113245/selection/5e9b625d4cdfd50931e6256d13df63e909e67d24a16ceb2dd816381e072bf2c8" "q-113245/selection/e07c611192af075822ecf1844fc9b9bd50dbccd83259e0c40b56147e9677b780" "q-113245/selection/2b6b5b63fb8ecaea967cd7ac2863ce8bd58656d3ccc4ec1b14aec4077dcfb3c4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-113245" :question/id #uuid "ed379096-4def-51e1-8cd6-e568b470e309" :question/math-academy-id "q-113245" :question/problem "The equation ${x}^{2}-6x+34=0$ can be written in the form $(x+p)^{2}=q.$ Find $p+q,$ and solve the equation." :question/worked-solution "We first move the constant to the right-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-6x+34 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-6x & =-34\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we complete the square on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-6x & =-34 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2\\cdot 3x+{3}^{2}-{3}^{2} & =-34 \\\\ (x-3)^{2}-9 & =-34 \\\\ (x-3)^{2} & =-25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=-3,\\,q=-25,$ and $p+q=-28.$\n\nFinally, we solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-3)^{2} & =-25 \\\\ x-3 & =\\pm \\sqrt{-25} \\\\ x-3 & =\\pm 5\\,\\text{i} \\\\ x & =3\\pm 5\\,\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has two solutions, $x=3+5\\,\\text{i}$ and $x=3-5\\,\\text{i}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-113245/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a9c8c1d8-2662-5c15-b084-084f9e930141"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-113245"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-218478"] :question/worked-solution "First, we write the equation in standard form by bringing all of the terms to the left-hand side. This gives the equation\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-2x+50=0.\n$$\n\nWe can find the roots of a quadratic equation using the quadratic formula:\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{-b\\pm \\sqrt{{b}^{2}-4ac}}{2a}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the coefficients are $a=1,\\,b=-2,$ and $c=50.$ Substituting these values into the quadratic formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{-(-2)\\pm \\sqrt{(-2)^{2}-4(1)(50)}}{2(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pm \\sqrt{4-200}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pm \\sqrt{-196}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pm 14\\,\\text{i}}{2} \\\\  & =1\\pm 7\\,\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has two solutions, $x=1+7\\,\\text{i}$ and $x=1-7\\,\\text{i}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
